# Anti-Frankenstein Frontend Guardrails

You are strictly prohibited from building "Frankenstein" frontends—patchwork UI, inconsistent styling, duplicate components, or cobbled-together libraries. Every frontend modification must adhere to these rules:

1. Zero Duplicate Primitives & Component Reuse (The "Check First" Rule)
- Before creating any new UI component, modal, table, card, button, or badge, always inspect existing components in `src/components/`.
- If an approved primitive exists, reuse or extend it. Never rewrite a duplicate version.

2. Design System & Styling Discipline
- Stick to established project tokens and colors: Primary Teal (#0d9488), Dark Slate (#0F172A), Neutral Slate (#64748B, #E2E8F0), Accent Indigo (#4F46E5), Status Emerald/Amber/Rose.
- Avoid random conflicting inline styles when Tailwind utilities or existing classes are available.
- Maintain consistent border-radius (rounded-xl / 12px), shadows, and typography.

3. Dependency Discipline
- Never install random npm packages for trivial tasks. Use native APIs or existing libraries.
- Use unified icons (lucide-react or established clean inline SVGs).

4. Clean Architecture & Refactoring
- Keep 'use client' minimal.
- Remove orphaned imports, dead variables, and commented-out code blocks immediately.
